platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"The intended installer edit, bounded verification files, restart proof, mandated restart, and subsequent cleanup all had clear roles. The only unnecessary mutation was the first malformed permission-test setup, which created and changed modes on temporary test directories but tested the parent directory's restrictive mode rather than the intended locked destination; it was fully reverted by its trap (cmd-eef9a324ec8b4a36). The corrected test followed. Final evidence shows the persistent proof removed, no failed services, no new exposure, and healthy package state. Lifecycle differences in temporary systemd directories and socket PIDs are expected consequences of the restart, not residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eef9a324ec8b4a36","cmd-f250a19ddedc4914","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: pre-restart functionality and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot identity changed, system state recovered to running, installed data and launcher behavior were revalidated, and the fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot transition.","limitations":["Lifecycle inspection is bounded to the supplied inventories and bundle listing, so unrelated filesystem changes outside those captures cannot be exhaustively excluded. No captured evidence otherwise indicates such changes."]}
